 "why_this_axis": "v01 measured: info_adaptivity 0.0135 over d_mean~0.55 => d_rel ~2.4%; g2_cls0 vs full flipped only 8/2000 predictions while g2_off flipped 329/2000 => ~97.6% of the field effect was plain isotropic diffusion and the \"information-guided\" part was inert. Cause: conv1x1 sat in the weight-decayed group, so wd (5e-4 x 0.1 x 62k steps = e^-3.1) shrank its weights ~22x and the map converged to sigmoid(0)=0.5. Dividing by the per-sample rms makes the loss exactly scale-invariant in ||w||, so wd becomes a mathematical no-op on the map's spatial contrast: collapse is structurally impossible, not tuned away.",
